load @term/seed/code/structure/function/binary
  find binary-function

# Convolution: the operation that blends two functions by sliding one across the other and accumulating the overlap, the
# multiplication of signals, of probability distributions, and of polynomials. It turns into ordinary multiplication
# under the Fourier transform, and it is how a local rule on a grid spreads its effect. The form carries the underlying
# binary operation.
form convolution
  link operation, like binary-function
